# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Line endings must NEVER be rewritten for the LightGBM ranker artifacts.
#
# LightGBM's text model parser is line-based and rejects CRLF outright. Worse,
# the failure surfaces as a native abort() (STATUS_STACK_BUFFER_OVERRUN) that
# terminates the whole process rather than raising a catchable exception — so a
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true silently prevents the AI service from
# starting, costing the entire learned-ranker edge.
#
# ORDERING MATTERS: in .gitattributes the LAST matching pattern wins, so these
# `-text` rules must come AFTER the broad defaults below, or they are ignored.
# Verify with: git check-attr text -- backend/ai_service/ranker_model.txt
#              → should print "text: unset"

# ── Broad defaults (must precede the specific overrides) ─────────────────────
* text=auto
*.py text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# ── Model artifacts: never line-ending converted ────────────────────────────
backend/ai_service/ranker_model.txt -text
backend/ai_service/ranker_meta.json -text
**/ranker_model.txt -text
**/ranker_meta.json -text
*.onnx -text
*.bin -text

# ── Binary assets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.pdf binary
*.pkl binary
*.joblib binary
